commit fc9df2c8a8b6dbe0c8fd9ec07ead2a406447a48a
Author: jingjiangze <1689170897@qq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 23:46:26 2026 +0800

    perf: delta public frames bounded by a periodic full anchor
    
    Step ④ of docs/ws-link-compression-next.md, on top of the compact baseline: a connection that declared hello.pubDelta gets delta hot frames when the match runs SP_PUB_SYNC=delta (the doc's switch, default full = complete frames exactly as before). A delta carries only the top-level keys that changed and, within players[], only the changed players and their changed keys; a cleared per-player key (pendingLp / uniteLeft) travels as an explicit null so the client's per-player merge can never keep a stale value. The chain is per recipient and rebuilt by every full baseline (start, _resync, reconnect); a complete anchor frame (no full marker; bounded by pubAnchorFrames=50 deltas / pubAnchorMs=30s, engine overrides for tests) heals a missed frame, and a delta with nothing new is not sent at all. Client: hello.pubDelta, players[] merged per player (public/js/main.js mergePlayers). Contracts pinned by test/match/ws-public-compact.test.js (per-recipient divergence, delta application, anchor cadence, missed-frame healing, cleared value, SP_PUB_SYNC=full fallback) and the lobby routing tests.

